# PROM (Oct 28): Grok's bench + hydrant candidates — they lost the side-by-side to the hand-drawn pieces (docs/harbor.md#prom); the
# sources stay on the laptop only (27–55 MB each), the bake recipe (scripts/bake/promenade.mjs) can re-render their looks
art/models/promenade/**/*.glb

# SKY-A (Oct 30): the F-22 model (25 MB — sources > ~20 MB stay on the laptop; scripts/bake/f22.mjs re-bakes it; credits.txt beside it is kept)
art/models/f22/*.glb
art/models/tree/*.glb
art/models/mothman/*.glb
art/models/blackbird/*.glb

# ATM-A (Oct 31): Grok's weather sounds — the originals (13 WAVs, ~140 MB, some Sonniss: never offered as stand-alone downloads) stay
# out of the public repo; scripts/add-city-sfx.py makes the shipped web copies in audio/city/; credits.txt + claude-notes.txt beside them kept
art/city-sfx/weather/*.wav
# ATM-C (Oct 31): Grok's thunder — the 9 originals (~50 MB; close-1, mid-1 + the deep slam are Sonniss) the same way
art/city-sfx/thunder/*.wav
# PART 10 (Oct 31): Grok's fireworks sounds — the 26 originals + 10 alternates (~120 MB; launch-1, crackle-1, whistle-1, crowd-2 + two
# alternates are Sonniss: never offered as stand-alone downloads) the same way; credits.txt + claude-notes.txt kept
art/city-sfx/fireworks/*.wav
art/city-sfx/fireworks/alternates/*.wav
# WINDOWS (Nov 1): Grok's juggler sounds — the originals + alternates (SB011 is Sonniss, one Mixkit: never stand-alone downloads) the same way
art/city-sfx/juggler/*.wav
art/city-sfx/juggler/alternates/*.wav
# CITY CONTROLS A (Nov 2): Grok's radio desk sounds — the originals (Sonniss + CC0 + Mixkit: never stand-alone downloads) the same way
art/city-sfx/radio/*.wav
art/city-sfx/radio/*.flac
